    {% comment %} ───────── The work ───────── {% endcomment %}
    <section class="stack">
      <h2>The work</h2>
      <p>
        The work runs across distributed systems at serious scale: satellite
        data and GIS, soft real-time pipelines in the critical path of ad-tech
        and fin-tech, services that have to behave the same under hundredfold
        load. Different domains, similar shape. The requirement is correctness
        under contention. The deliverable is something the next person can read.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most engagements start the same way &mdash; a system that needs to be
        designed before it's built, or a codebase that has outgrown the team
        that wrote it, or an organization that wants a senior pair of hands on
        the architecture for a season. The work is hands-on. Designs come with
        implementations. Implementations come with tests, observability, and a
        path to operate them.
      </p>
      <p>
        The materials run to the high-performance end &mdash; often Rust,
        Erlang, or Go. AWS, GCP, or on-site. Kafka or NATS for messaging; SQL,
        graph, or vector for storage. Fit to the problem, not to a stack.
        Functional by preference; pragmatic by practice.
      </p>
    </section>

